        "title": "Rhetoric - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Rhetoric is the art and science of persuasion through language. It is distinct from logic (which studies validity regardless of audience), linguistics (which studies language structure), and literature (which studies aesthetic uses of language). Rhetoric is practical — it asks: how do you move a specific audience to a specific belief or action using language?"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:rhetoric:00-overview, git-history:rhetoric:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:rhetoric:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "rhetoric",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rhetoric - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  RHETORIC — LANDSCAPE MAP                        |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  CLASSICAL SYSTEM (Aristotle, Cicero, Quintilian)               |\n|  Three Genres: Deliberative / Forensic / Epideictic             |\n|  Three Appeals: Logos (reason) / Ethos (character) / Pathos    |\n|  Five Canons: Inventio / Dispositio / Elocutio /                |\n|               Memoria / Actio                                    |\n|                                                                  |\n|  MODERN EXTENSIONS                                               |\n|  Argumentation theory (Toulmin model, informal logic)           |\n|  Political rhetoric and framing (Lakoff, Luntz)                 |\n|  Epideictic/ceremonial: eulogy, toast, commencement            |\n|  Digital rhetoric: social media, virality, memes               |\n|  Composition and pedagogy: writing process, genre              |\n|                                                                  |\n|  DIRECT PROFESSIONAL RELEVANCE (VP level)                       |\n|  Inventio: finding the right argument for the right audience   |\n|  Dispositio: document/presentation architecture                 |\n|  Ethos: credibility as a speaker and leader                     |\n|  Toulmin: every design doc is a Toulmin argument               |\n|  Framing: how you present technical work to non-technical exec  |\n|  Epideictic: eulogy, award, toast, commencement                 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
