        "id": "maxim:rhetoric:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "rhetoric",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rhetoric - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Aristotle distinguished three genres by time, audience, and purpose:"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#007",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:rhetoric:00-overview, git-history:rhetoric:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:rhetoric:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "rhetoric",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rhetoric - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHREE GENRES (SPECIES) OF RHETORIC\n-------------------------------------\nDELIBERATIVE (symbouleutikon)\n  Time: future\n  Audience: a legislative body or decision-maker\n  Purpose: advise on a course of action\n  Judgment: expedient/inexpedient; advantageous/harmful\n  Examples: legislative speeches, policy recommendations,\n    business strategy presentations, executive briefings\n  Your context: any presentation to leadership about\n    what to do next quarter/year"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#008",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:rhetoric:00-overview, git-history:rhetoric:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:rhetoric:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "rhetoric",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rhetoric - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FORENSIC (dikanikon)\n  Time: past\n  Audience: a judge or jury\n  Purpose: accuse or defend a person/organization\n  Judgment: just/unjust; guilty/not guilty\n  Examples: trial arguments, post-mortem reviews,\n    incident retrospectives, performance reviews\n  Your context: any review of what happened and who/what\n    is responsible"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:rhetoric:00-overview, git-history:rhetoric:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "rhetoric/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:rhetoric:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "rhetoric",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rhetoric - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EPIDEICTIC (epideiktikon)\n  Time: present\n  Audience: spectators/witnesses\n  Purpose: praise or blame; express shared values\n  Judgment: noble/base; honorable/dishonorable\n  Examples: eulogies, award speeches, toasts, commencement,\n    team recognition, product launch speeches\n  Your context: any speech that celebrates, honors,\n    or marks a communal moment\n```"
    },
    {
